[2026-03-14T23:12:30.965Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QEXhZt8qZGQF5Jxrr4tNqQ","type":"tool_result","content":"2343-- **Expected**: The modal closes. No new team is created. The teams list remains unchanged.\n2344-\n2345:#### Test: Close create team modal by clicking backdrop\n2346-- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open.\n2347-- **Action**: User clicks outside the modal (on the backdrop overlay)\n2348-- **Expected**: The modal closes without creating a team.\n2349-\n2350:#### Test: Create team modal form resets on reopen\n2351-- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/teams`. User previously opened the Create Team modal, entered some data, and cancelled.\n2352-- **Action**: User clicks \"Create Team\" button again\n2353-- **Expected**: The modal opens with all fields empty/reset. No residual data from the previous attempt is present.\n2354-\n2355:#### Test: Create team modal can be used multiple times in sequence\n2356-- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/teams`.\n2357-- **Action**: User clicks \"Create Team\", enters Name \"Team Alpha\", prefix \"ALPH\", clicks \"Create Team\". Then clicks \"Create Team\" again, enters Name \"Team Beta\", prefix \"BETA\", clicks \"Create Team\".\n2358-- **Expected**: Both teams are created. The teams page shows both new team cards. The modal opens cleanly with empty fields the second time.\n2359-\n2360:#### Test: Create team modal submits via Enter key\n2361-- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open. User has entered Name \"QA Team\" and Identifier prefix \"QA\".\n2362-- **Action**: User presses Enter while focused on the form\n--\n2365-### TeamSettings\n2366-\n2367:#### Test: Team settings page renders with editable fields\n2368-- **Initial state**: Workspace has a team \"Engineering\" with prefix \"ENG\" and description \"Core engineering team\". User clicks the \"Engineering\" team card on `/settings/teams`.\n2369-- **Expected**: The team settings view displays: Team name field showing \"Engineering\" (inline editable), Identifier prefix field showing \"ENG\" (inline editable), Description field showing \"Core engineering team\" (inline editable), and a \"Team Members\" section listing current members. A \"Back\" or navigation link to return to the teams list is visible. A \"Delete Team\" button is also present.\n2370-\n2371:#### Test: Inline edit team name\n2372-- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2373-- **Action**: User clicks on the team name field, changes it from \"Engineering\" to \"Platform Engineering\", and confirms (blur or Enter)\n2374-- **Expected**: The team name updates to \"Platform Engineering\". The change is persisted (reloading the page still shows \"Platform Engineering\"). The sidebar team section also reflects the updated name.\n2375-\n2376:#### Test: Inline edit team name with empty value rejected\n2377-- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2378-- **Action**: User clicks on the team name field, clears the value, and attempts to confirm\n2379-- **Expected**: A validation error is shown indicating the team name cannot be empty. The name reverts to \"Engineering\" or the error blocks the save.\n2380-\n2381:#### Test: Inline edit team identifier prefix\n2382-- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\" with prefix \"ENG\".\n2383-- **Action**: User clicks on the identifier prefix field, changes it to \"ENGR\", and confirms\n2384-- **Expected**: The identifier prefix updates to \"ENGR\". The change is persisted. Existing issues retain their original identifiers (e.g., \"ENG-42\" does not change), but new issues will use the new prefix \"ENGR\".\n2385-\n2386:#### Test: Inline edit team identifier prefix enforces uppercase and 2-5 char limit\n2387-- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\" with prefix \"ENG\".\n2388-- **Action**: User clicks on the identifier prefix field and enters \"a\" (lowercase, 1 char)\n2389-- **Expected**: The input is either auto-uppercased to \"A\" or rejected as lowercase. A validation error indicates the prefix must be 2-5 uppercase characters. The prefix reverts to \"ENG\" if the edit is not valid.\n2390-\n2391:#### Test: Inline edit team identifier prefix rejects duplicate prefix\n2392-- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\" with prefix \"ENG\". Another team \"Design\" has prefix \"DES\".\n2393-- **Action**: User changes the identifier prefix from \"ENG\" to \"DES\" and confirms\n2394-- **Expected**: An error is shown indicating the prefix \"DES\" is already in use by another team. The prefix reverts to \"ENG\" or the save is blocked.\n2395-\n2396:#### Test: Inline edit team description\n2397-- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\" with description \"Core engineering team\".\n2398-- **Action**: User clicks on the description field, changes it to \"Platform and infrastructure engineering\", and confirms\n2399-- **Expected**: The description updates to \"Platform and infrastructure engineering\". The change is persisted.\n2400-\n2401:#### Test: Inline edit team description can be cleared\n2402-- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\" with description \"Core engineering team\".\n2403-- **Action**: User clicks on the description field, clears all text, and confirms\n2404-- **Expected**: The description is cleared. The field shows a placeholder or empty state. No error is shown (description is optional).\n2405-\n2406:#### Test: Team members section lists all current team members\n2407-- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has 3 members: Alice, Bob, Carol. User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2408-- **Expected**: The Team Members section displays a list of 3 members. Each member row shows their avatar and name. An \"Add Member\" button is visible.\n2409-\n2410:#### Test: Add member to team via team settings\n2411-- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has 2 members. Workspace member \"David\" is not on this team. User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2412-- **Action**: User clicks \"Add Member\", selects \"David\" from the member selector, and confirms\n2413-- **Expected**: David is added to the team. The Team Members section now shows 3 members including David. The team card on the teams page reflects the updated member count. David's member row on the Members page (`/settings/members`) now includes an \"Engineering\" team badge.\n2414-\n2415:#### Test: Add member selector shows only non-team members\n2416-- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has members Alice and Bob. Workspace also has Carol and David who are not on this team. User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2417-- **Action**: User clicks \"Add Member\"\n2418-- **Expected**: The member selector dropdown shows only Carol and David (members not already on the team). Alice and Bob are not shown in the dropdown since they are already team members.\n2419-\n2420:#### Test: Remove member from team via team settings\n2421-- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has 3 members: Alice, Bob, Carol. User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2422-- **Action**: User clicks the remove button next to Carol's name in the Team Members list\n2423-- **Expected**: A confirmation prompt appears (e.g., \"Remove Carol from Engineering?\"). User confirms. Carol is removed from the team members list. The section now shows 2 members. Carol remains a workspace member but is no longer on the \"Engineering\" team. The team card member count decreases.\n2424-\n2425:#### Test: Cancel remove member from team\n2426-- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has 3 members. User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2427-- **Action**: User clicks the remove button next to a member's name, then clicks \"Cancel\" in the confirmation prompt\n2428-- **Expected**: The member is not removed. The Team Members list still shows 3 members.\n2429-\n2430:#### Test: Team members section shows empty state when team has no members\n2431-- **Initial state**: Team \"QA\" has no members. User is on team settings for \"QA\".\n2432-- **Expected**: The Team Members section shows an empty state message (e.g., \"No members yet. Add members to this team.\"). The \"Add Member\" button is visible.\n2433-\n2434:#### Test: Add member to team can be done multiple times in sequence\n2435-- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has 1 member. Workspace has 3 other members (Bob, Carol, David). User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2436-- **Action**: User adds Bob via \"Add Member\", then adds Carol via \"Add Member\" again\n2437-- **Expected**: Both Bob and Carol are added to the team. The Team Members section now shows 3 members. The \"Add Member\" selector correctly filters out already-added members each time.\n2438-\n2439:#### Test: Delete team button shows confirmation dialog\n2440-- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2441-- **Action**: User clicks the \"Delete Team\" button"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e08fcd51-8932-4cb2-94f1-10b89baa0f1a","uuid":"73ba7789-5f43-4d94-b943-f0f64a3dd13f","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"2343-- **Expected**: The modal closes. No new team is created. The teams list remains unchanged.\n2344-\n2345:#### Test: Close create team modal by clicking backdrop\n2346-- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open.\n2347-- **Action**: User clicks outside the modal (on the backdrop overlay)\n2348-- **Expected**: The modal closes without creating a team.\n2349-\n2350:#### Test: Create team modal form resets on reopen\n2351-- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/teams`. User previously opened the Create Team modal, entered some data, and cancelled.\n2352-- **Action**: User clicks \"Create Team\" button again\n2353-- **Expected**: The modal opens with all fields empty/reset. No residual data from the previous attempt is present.\n2354-\n2355:#### Test: Create team modal can be used multiple times in sequence\n2356-- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/teams`.\n2357-- **Action**: User clicks \"Create Team\", enters Name \"Team Alpha\", prefix \"ALPH\", clicks \"Create Team\". Then clicks \"Create Team\" again, enters Name \"Team Beta\", prefix \"BETA\", clicks \"Create Team\".\n2358-- **Expected**: Both teams are created. The teams page shows both new team cards. The modal opens cleanly with empty fields the second time.\n2359-\n2360:#### Test: Create team modal submits via Enter key\n2361-- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open. User has entered Name \"QA Team\" and Identifier prefix \"QA\".\n2362-- **Action**: User presses Enter while focused on the form\n--\n2365-### TeamSettings\n2366-\n2367:#### Test: Team settings page renders with editable fields\n2368-- **Initial state**: Workspace has a team \"Engineering\" with prefix \"ENG\" and description \"Core engineering team\". User clicks the \"Engineering\" team card on `/settings/teams`.\n2369-- **Expected**: The team settings view displays: Team name field showing \"Engineering\" (inline editable), Identifier prefix field showing \"ENG\" (inline editable), Description field showing \"Core engineering team\" (inline editable), and a \"Team Members\" section listing current members. A \"Back\" or navigation link to return to the teams list is visible. A \"Delete Team\" button is also present.\n2370-\n2371:#### Test: Inline edit team name\n2372-- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2373-- **Action**: User clicks on the team name field, changes it from \"Engineering\" to \"Platform Engineering\", and confirms (blur or Enter)\n2374-- **Expected**: The team name updates to \"Platform Engineering\". The change is persisted (reloading the page still shows \"Platform Engineering\"). The sidebar team section also reflects the updated name.\n2375-\n2376:#### Test: Inline edit team name with empty value rejected\n2377-- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2378-- **Action**: User clicks on the team name field, clears the value, and attempts to confirm\n2379-- **Expected**: A validation error is shown indicating the team name cannot be empty. The name reverts to \"Engineering\" or the error blocks the save.\n2380-\n2381:#### Test: Inline edit team identifier prefix\n2382-- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\" with prefix \"ENG\".\n2383-- **Action**: User clicks on the identifier prefix field, changes it to \"ENGR\", and confirms\n2384-- **Expected**: The identifier prefix updates to \"ENGR\". The change is persisted. Existing issues retain their original identifiers (e.g., \"ENG-42\" does not change), but new issues will use the new prefix \"ENGR\".\n2385-\n2386:#### Test: Inline edit team identifier prefix enforces uppercase and 2-5 char limit\n2387-- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\" with prefix \"ENG\".\n2388-- **Action**: User clicks on the identifier prefix field and enters \"a\" (lowercase, 1 char)\n2389-- **Expected**: The input is either auto-uppercased to \"A\" or rejected as lowercase. A validation error indicates the prefix must be 2-5 uppercase characters. The prefix reverts to \"ENG\" if the edit is not valid.\n2390-\n2391:#### Test: Inline edit team identifier prefix rejects duplicate prefix\n2392-- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\" with prefix \"ENG\". Another team \"Design\" has prefix \"DES\".\n2393-- **Action**: User changes the identifier prefix from \"ENG\" to \"DES\" and confirms\n2394-- **Expected**: An error is shown indicating the prefix \"DES\" is already in use by another team. The prefix reverts to \"ENG\" or the save is blocked.\n2395-\n2396:#### Test: Inline edit team description\n2397-- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\" with description \"Core engineering team\".\n2398-- **Action**: User clicks on the description field, changes it to \"Platform and infrastructure engineering\", and confirms\n2399-- **Expected**: The description updates to \"Platform and infrastructure engineering\". The change is persisted.\n2400-\n2401:#### Test: Inline edit team description can be cleared\n2402-- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\" with description \"Core engineering team\".\n2403-- **Action**: User clicks on the description field, clears all text, and confirms\n2404-- **Expected**: The description is cleared. The field shows a placeholder or empty state. No error is shown (description is optional).\n2405-\n2406:#### Test: Team members section lists all current team members\n2407-- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has 3 members: Alice, Bob, Carol. User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2408-- **Expected**: The Team Members section displays a list of 3 members. Each member row shows their avatar and name. An \"Add Member\" button is visible.\n2409-\n2410:#### Test: Add member to team via team settings\n2411-- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has 2 members. Workspace member \"David\" is not on this team. User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2412-- **Action**: User clicks \"Add Member\", selects \"David\" from the member selector, and confirms\n2413-- **Expected**: David is added to the team. The Team Members section now shows 3 members including David. The team card on the teams page reflects the updated member count. David's member row on the Members page (`/settings/members`) now includes an \"Engineering\" team badge.\n2414-\n2415:#### Test: Add member selector shows only non-team members\n2416-- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has members Alice and Bob. Workspace also has Carol and David who are not on this team. User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2417-- **Action**: User clicks \"Add Member\"\n2418-- **Expected**: The member selector dropdown shows only Carol and David (members not already on the team). Alice and Bob are not shown in the dropdown since they are already team members.\n2419-\n2420:#### Test: Remove member from team via team settings\n2421-- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has 3 members: Alice, Bob, Carol. User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2422-- **Action**: User clicks the remove button next to Carol's name in the Team Members list\n2423-- **Expected**: A confirmation prompt appears (e.g., \"Remove Carol from Engineering?\"). User confirms. Carol is removed from the team members list. The section now shows 2 members. Carol remains a workspace member but is no longer on the \"Engineering\" team. The team card member count decreases.\n2424-\n2425:#### Test: Cancel remove member from team\n2426-- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has 3 members. User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2427-- **Action**: User clicks the remove button next to a member's name, then clicks \"Cancel\" in the confirmation prompt\n2428-- **Expected**: The member is not removed. The Team Members list still shows 3 members.\n2429-\n2430:#### Test: Team members section shows empty state when team has no members\n2431-- **Initial state**: Team \"QA\" has no members. User is on team settings for \"QA\".\n2432-- **Expected**: The Team Members section shows an empty state message (e.g., \"No members yet. Add members to this team.\"). The \"Add Member\" button is visible.\n2433-\n2434:#### Test: Add member to team can be done multiple times in sequence\n2435-- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has 1 member. Workspace has 3 other members (Bob, Carol, David). User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2436-- **Action**: User adds Bob via \"Add Member\", then adds Carol via \"Add Member\" again\n2437-- **Expected**: Both Bob and Carol are added to the team. The Team Members section now shows 3 members. The \"Add Member\" selector correctly filters out already-added members each time.\n2438-\n2439:#### Test: Delete team button shows confirmation dialog\n2440-- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2441-- **Action**: User clicks the \"Delete Team\" button","numLines":98}}
